The Player source is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE
in this directory; D-015 decided Apache-2.0 over MIT, D-064 confirmed it).

Two flavors (D-126 option A):

- core (this notice): the main Apache-2.0 release. It ships no GPL code.
- full (see NOTICE.full and LICENSE.full): adds the bundled sherpa-onnx
  speech runtime with static espeak-ng (GPL-3.0) and is distributed as a
  GPL-3.0 combined work, with its license text and written source offer
  inside the APK.

Open-source libraries each flavor uses are listed with their versions
and licenses in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md (core) and
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.full.md (full); the same lists are shown in the app
under Settings > Licenses (per flavor, matching each build).

The voice models that made the audiobooks (Kokoro-82M, espeak-ng,
en_core_web_sm) run on the PC (Scribe) and are not bundled in the core
app. Piper voice packs are files you copy yourself and never ship in
either APK; each pack has its own license.
